{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791700234,"nonce":"Oduz8QXhM7+1HbDHjc4GEQME8Zc=","title":"Base UI switch knob and panels move by mechanisms ashui already replaced","message":"The switch knob moved by `justify-content` and a layout animation. It flew in from a hidden tab panel's box and stopped animating in a window. ashui slides its thumb with a `transform: translateX(travel)` transition on --ease-spring, composed with the press scale: paint only, nothing to measure, nothing to fly in from.\n\nCollapsible and accordion panels were `display: none` when hidden, so opening began from a box of no size, and closing ended with a jump as the panel's gap went. ashui lays closed content out at height 0, so opening and closing are both a change of size.\n\npresence asked for the panel's motion inside the effect pass, before the pass had written `data-closed`.\n\nbase-ui-components ran without the Base UI sheet, so its panel never folded and \"it is seen folding away\" passed only on a leftover opening move; base-ui-motion's fold check watched only the strip below the panel, which moves at once, and passed only on the end jump.\n\nChanges: transform knob with travel tokens (--space-4, --space-5; lg track 46px), hidden panels laid out at no height, presence asks after the pass and not after its owner ended, tests watch the panel itself and load the sheet; wiki.mjs presses a switch and closes a panel with window frames.","files":null}]}